+# content_patterns above. The path_patterns rows and sensitive_path_list still apply in full;
+# this suppresses ONE signal, never a protection.
+#
+# Why it exists: content_patterns look for ordinary English — "consent", "price", "timeout",
+# "privacy policy". In prose those words are the SUBJECT, not the change: a documentation page
+# describing a consent flow is not a consent flow, yet a one-word typo fix in it scored impact
+# `high` and routed to the full pipeline. Exclude the file types whose content is narrative.
+#
+# Fail-closed by absence: leave the key out and nothing is excluded, which is the pre-3.4.1
+# behaviour. Do NOT exclude a path whose markdown is executable instruction (a skill, an agent
